# `ekwo init` writes this next to wherever it was run, and running it from a
# clone is the ordinary way to install from source. It holds no secret — the
# project URL, the country, the schema version — but it is one installation's
# and not this repository's, and a `git add -A` after an install would publish
# which project the person installed into.
ekwo.json

# The site's build. `dist/` above already covers its pages; this is the second
# folder its build writes, holding the bundled prerender script that fills the
# template. Both are output, and both are rebuilt by one command.
apps/site/.prerender/
